{"id": "C-001", "date": "2026-06-08", "work": "/investigations/blood-routes/", "summary": "The report's night-time crash statistic was published as 97.13% (derived from a dataset later found to contain ~95% synthetic padding); it was corrected to 41.56% (RSF Dhaka Annual Report 2025 basis) on 2026-06-08, after the pipeline retracted the original figure on 2026-06-03. The change was made in commit 527d0a4 without a log entry at the time.", "amended": "Night-time share of fatal Dhaka crashes corrected 97.13% → 41.56% (10pm–6am window)."}
{"id": "C-002", "date": "2026-09-03", "work": "/investigations/blood-routes/", "summary": "The Eid-ul-Adha 2025 timeline entry described a '29% YoY surge' in road fatalities. The report's own timeline data (312 deaths in 2025 vs 262 in 2024) yields a 19.08% increase, not 29%. The 29% figure appears to have been inherited from a contemporaneous RSF report framing rather than computed from the published series.", "amended": "Eid-ul-Adha 2025 timeline description corrected to 'Sharp 19% year-on-year rise (312 vs 262 in 2024)'."}
{"id": "C-003", "date": "2026-09-03", "work": "/investigations/the-impunity-machine/", "summary": "A note disclosing that the Bangladesh 0.46% conviction rate and the UK/India/South Africa comparator rates use different denominators (all complaints registered at One-Stop Crisis Centres vs prosecuted trials in court) was added to the comparison section after initial publication (commit 36177f6, 2026-05-26).", "amended": "Cross-jurisdictional comparison chart now carries the denominator note; the comparison must not be read as like-for-like conviction rates."}
{"id": "C-004", "date": "2026-09-03", "work": "/investigations/the-impunity-machine/", "summary": "The published source count of 91 named sources overstated the archived source registry, which contains 65 entries (54 CONFIRMED, 11 PROBABLE). 27 IDs in the S-01..S-91 sequence (including S-26, S-27, S-28) had no registry entries.", "amended": "Source count corrected to 65 across the report, detailed report, methodology page, manifest, and evidence page. The S-26 citation was re-mapped to registry entry S-37 (UNFPA/BBS VAW Survey 2024 Highlights, exact content match); the S-27/S-28 parenthetical citations were removed (no registry equivalents exist; source names retained without dead IDs)."}
